From 151145048ed22ab4d7ca1cc8abe8b57702bccdf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:54:56 +0800
Subject: mm/memcontrol: fix data-race on reading jiffies_64

From: Jiayuan Chen <jiayuan.chen@linux.dev>

[ Upstream commit c20cf1c3c8cdd98618d6fcc794003a0e003ae858 ]

KCSAN reported a data-race between tick_do_update_jiffies64() updating
jiffies_64 and mem_cgroup_flush_stats_ratelimited() reading it directly.

Unlike jiffies, jiffies_64 is not volatile, so raw reads are plain
accesses and can even be torn on 32-bit.  Use get_jiffies_64() instead,
and fix the same pattern in mem_cgroup_flush_foreign().

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20260827025457.116191-1-jiayuan.chen@linux.dev
Fixes: 508bed884767 ("mm: memcg: change flush_next_time to flush_last_time")
Fixes: 97b27821b485 ("writeback, memcg: Implement foreign dirty flushing")
Signed-off-by: Jiayuan Chen <jiayuan.chen@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reported-by: syzbot+ced4d9a8cadb5ef3adae@syzkaller.appspotmail.com
Acked-by: Muchun Song <muchun.song@linux.dev>
Acked-by: Johannes Weiner <hannes@cmpxchg.org>
Acked-by: Michal Hocko <mhocko@suse.com>
Cc: Chris Li <chrisl@kernel.org>
Cc: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Cc: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Cc: Roman Gushchin <roman.gushchin@linux.dev>
Cc: Shakeel Butt <shakeel.butt@linux.dev>
Cc: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>

[ sashal: Applied the same get_jiffies_64() conversion to the older flush_next_time code, which has no flush_last_time or READ_ONCE; dropped the cosmetic whitespace change. ]

Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 mm/memcontrol.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/memcontrol.c b/mm/memcontrol.c
index 4a841e2a4853c..ae060f1772b11 100644
--- a/mm/memcontrol.c
+++ b/mm/memcontrol.c
@@ -631,7 +631,7 @@ static void __mem_cgroup_flush_stats(void)
 	if (!spin_trylock_irqsave(&stats_flush_lock, flag))
 		return;
 
-	flush_next_time = jiffies_64 + 2*FLUSH_TIME;
+	flush_next_time = get_jiffies_64() + 2*FLUSH_TIME;
 	cgroup_rstat_flush_irqsafe(root_mem_cgroup->css.cgroup);
 	atomic_set(&stats_flush_threshold, 0);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&stats_flush_lock, flag);
@@ -645,7 +645,7 @@ void mem_cgroup_flush_stats(void)
 
 void mem_cgroup_flush_stats_delayed(void)
 {
-	if (time_after64(jiffies_64, flush_next_time))
+	if (time_after64(get_jiffies_64(), flush_next_time))
 		mem_cgroup_flush_stats();
 }
 
@@ -4732,7 +4732,7 @@ void mem_cgroup_flush_foreign(struct bdi_writeback *wb)
 {
 	struct mem_cgroup *memcg = mem_cgroup_from_css(wb->memcg_css);
 	unsigned long intv = msecs_to_jiffies(dirty_expire_interval * 10);
-	u64 now = jiffies_64;
+	u64 now = get_jiffies_64();
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < MEMCG_CGWB_FRN_CNT; i++) {
-- 
